# scripts/tool-versions.env — SINGLE SOURCE for this repo's pinned gate-tool versions.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by two consumers:
#   • .github/workflows/ci.yml — a "Load pinned tool versions" step cats this into
#     $GITHUB_ENV, so CI installs exactly these and no version literal is left in the YAML.
#   • .github/actions/… — the shared composite action this repo borrows from dotfiles-core
#     (dotgibson/dotfiles-core/.github/actions/setup-core-tools@v7) reads BOTH the
#     *_VERSION and the *_SHA256 from $GITHUB_ENV and verifies each download before
#     installing it. That verification is the real supply-chain control: a tampered or
#     MITM'd asset fails the build instead of executing in the gate.
#
# Plain KEY=VALUE, no spaces around `=`, no `v` prefix — so this both `source`s in bash
# AND appends straight to $GITHUB_ENV.
#
# SHORTER THAN CORE'S ON PURPOSE. shellcheck, actionlint, gitleaks and markdownlint are
# not pinned here because this repo does not install them: .github/workflows/lint.yml is a
# three-line caller of dotfiles-core's reusable lint gate, which brings its own pins. The
# tools below are the ones only this repo runs.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Neovim. THE floor for the whole fleet, not merely this gate's convenience: nvim-treesitter
# is pinned to `main`, which requires 0.12. dotfiles-core's PORTING-MATRIX.md renders that
# number for every OS repo, and after the split it is a property of THIS repo (#1126).
NVIM_VERSION=0.12.5
NVIM_SHA256=bce0f56eda1f1b1db6eee8f4133d7a38813ea07933837dd1777411ca384c6875

# luacheck. A luarocks build, not a release asset, so there is no hash to pin — the CI leg
# installs it with `luarocks --local install luacheck "$LUACHECK_VERSION"`.
# PIN THE INTERPRETER TOO, at the install site: luarocks now defaults to Lua 5.5, and
# luacheck 1.2.0 (its last release) fails to even LOAD under it — 5.5 made some locals
# const, which trips "attempt to assign to const variable" inside luacheck's own source.
LUACHECK_VERSION=1.2.0

# stylua. NEW HERE — dotfiles-core pins no stylua at all, because it wired none: stylua
# existed there only as a Mason-installed formatter inside nvim/lua/gerrrt/plugins/conform.lua.
# The audit's stylua leg is ADVISORY for now; scripts/audit/10-lua.sh §1b says why, and what
# has to land before it can become a gate.
# The hash is of the release ZIP (stylua-linux-x86_64.zip), not of the extracted binary.
STYLUA_VERSION=2.5.2
STYLUA_SHA256=bcb0d855e91f102f28a370e850f8566b3b44b79e6274d806ea5246837c0fd5ab
